{"id":"sms-voice","corpus":"aws","title":"AWS End User Messaging SMS","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sms-voice/latest/userguide/what-is-sms-mms.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"AWS End User Messaging SMS"},{"kind":"p","text":"The SMS, MMS, and voice (text to speech) features of Amazon Pinpoint are now called AWS End User Messaging."},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS End User Messaging SMS is an application-to-person (A2P) SMS, MMS, RCS, and voice messaging service which provides the global scale, resiliency, and flexibility required to deliver messaging in any web, mobile, or business applications. SMS messages are used for their most important and urgent communications as SMS proves to be the most effective and ubiquitous communication channel available. Customers prioritize time critical and must-deliver use-cases such as one-time password (OTP) login and authentication, marketing messages, citizen outreach, delivery status updates, or appointment reminders to name a few."},{"kind":"p","text":"Multimedia messaging service (MMS) is an extension of SMS that provides the ability to send media messages to a mobile phone which includes image, audio, text, or video files. You can use MMS to improve engagement through a variety of branding, workflow, and marketing use cases."},{"kind":"p","text":"Rich Communication Services (RCS) for business provides verified brand identity, delivery receipts, and improved messaging performance for your messages. AWS End User Messaging SMS supports sending text messages via RCS with automatic SMS fallback when RCS is unavailable. You create an AWS RCS Agent to represent your brand, and use phone pools to enable seamless RCS-to-SMS fallback. For more information, see RCS messaging."},{"kind":"p","text":"The information in this user guide is intended for all AWS End User Messaging SMS users, including marketers, business users, and developers. This guide contains information that's especially helpful for users who mainly interact with AWS End User Messaging SMS by using the AWS Management Console."},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS End User Messaging SMS uses the pinpoint-sms-voice-v2 API namespace."},{"kind":"p","text":"There are several other documents that are companions to this document. The following documents provide reference information related to the AWS End User Messaging SMS APIs:"},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS End User Messaging SMS and Voice v2 API"},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS End User Messaging SMS and Voice v2 AWS CLI reference"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS End User Messaging SMS includes an API (called the AWS End User Messaging SMS and Voice v2 API) that was designed for sending SMS, MMS and voice messages. While the Amazon Pinpoint API is focused on sending messages through scheduled and event-driven campaigns and journeys, the AWS End User Messaging SMS and Voice v2 API provides dedicated features and capabilities for sending SMS, MMS, and voice messages directly to individual recipients. You can use AWS End User Messaging SMS and Voice API v2 independently of the Amazon Pinpoint campaign and journey features, or you can use both at the same time to accommodate different use cases. If you already use Amazon Pinpoint to send SMS, MMS, or voice messages, your account is already configured to use this API. Here are some key feature differences between the two APIs."},{"kind":"p","text":"This API is a good solution for users who have a multi-tenant architecture, such as Independent Software Vendors (ISVs). This API can be used to establish that event data, origination phone numbers, and opt-out lists are separated for different tenants."},{"kind":"p","text":"When you use the SMS and Voice v2 API, we recommend that you set up phone pools, configuration sets and event destinations. The SMS and Voice v2 API doesn't automatically emit event data for the messages that you send. Setting up event destinations to capture important event data, such as message delivery and failure events."},{"kind":"p","text":"Version 2 of this API was preceded by Version 1. If you currently use Version 1 of this API, it will continue to be available, and you can continue to use it. However, if you migrate to Version 2, you will gain additional features, such as the ability to create pools of phone numbers, request new phone numbers programmatically, and enable or disable certain capabilities of phone numbers."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Are you a first-time AWS End User Messaging SMS user?"},{"kind":"p","text":"If you're using AWS End User Messaging SMS for the first time, we recommend that you first read the following sections:"},{"kind":"li","text":"How Short Message Service (SMS) works"},{"kind":"li","text":"Tutorial for sending a message using AWS End User Messaging SMS"},{"kind":"h2","text":"Features of AWS End User Messaging SMS"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS End User Messaging SMS provides the following features and capabilities:"}],"lemmas":{"ends":["end","ends"],"ended":["ended","end"],"ending":["ending","end"],"messaging":["messaging","message"],"messagings":["messaging","messagings"],"voices":["voice","voices"],"voiced":["voiced","voice"],"voicing":["voicing","voice"],"texts":["text","texts"],"speeches":["speech","speeches"],"features":["feature","features"],"featuring":["featuring","feature"],"featured":["featured","feature"],"amazons":["amazon","amazons"],"pinpoints":["pinpoint","pinpoints"],"called":["called","call"],"calleds":["calleds","called"],"calls":["call","calls"],"calling":["calling","call"],"people":["people","person"],"persons":["person","persons"],"serviced":["serviced","service"],"servicing":["servicing","service"],"provides":["provides","provide"],"provided":["provided","provide"],"providing":["providing","provide"],"globals":["globals","global"],"scales":["scale","scales"],"scaling":["scaling","scale"],"scaled":["scaled","scale"],"resiliencies":["resiliency","resiliencies"],"flexibilities":["flexibility","fle